---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Follow a build of this site to its end.

\e[1mUsage\e[0m: \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mwatch\e[0m \e[36m[OPTIONS]\e[0m \e[36m[BUILD]\e[0m

\e[1mExamples\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mwatch\e[0m  \e[2m# \e[0mFollow the build that is running, or wait for the next

\e[1mArguments\e[0m
  \e[36m[BUILD]\e[0m  The build to follow, by the start of its id. Without one, the build
           that is running or queued, or else the next one the site starts

\e[1mOptions\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --wait\e[0m \e[36m<SECONDS>\e[0m  Seconds to wait before stopping; the build keeps going
                        on the server \e[2m[default: 300]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --poll\e[0m \e[36m<MS>\e[0m       Milliseconds between two looks at the site
                        \e[2m[default: 1000]\e[0m

\e[1mAccount\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --api\e[0m \e[36m<URL>\e[0m          The API's address, `\e[1m\e[36mhttp://host[:port]\e[0m`;
                           `\e[1m\e[36maccount.api\e[0m` in the config file \e[2m[env: INK_API]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --site\e[0m \e[36m<ID>\e[0m          The site's id; `\e[1m\e[36maccount.site\e[0m` in the config file
                           \e[2m[env: INK_SITE]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --org\e[0m \e[36m<ID>\e[0m           Act as this organization, by its id: the site is one
                           of its sites, and the key's role there is what is
                           checked. See `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36morg\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlist\e[0m` \e[2m[env: INK_ORG]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --timeout\e[0m \e[36m<SECONDS>\e[0m  Seconds one call may take \e[2m[default: 30]\e[0m
                           \e[2m[env: INK_TIMEOUT]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --retries\e[0m \e[36m<N>\e[0m        How many more times a call that is safe to repeat is
                           tried when the network fails \e[2m[default: 2]\e[0m
                           \e[2m[env: INK_RETRIES]\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36m    --retry-wait\e[0m \e[36m<MS>\e[0m    Milliseconds before the first retry; each wait is
                           twice the one before \e[2m[default: 500]\e[0m
                           \e[2m[env: INK_RETRY_WAIT]\e[0m

\e[1mNotes\e[0m
  Follows a build to its end: the one named, the one running, or the next the
  site starts. Prints the deploy id.

\e[1mExit codes\e[0m
  0  Done: the deploy is live
  1  The build was refused: the site does not build
  2  Wrong usage: the folder is linked to no site, or the folder cannot be read
  3  Not signed in, or the signature was refused
  4  The API could not be reached, the build failed or the wait ran out; safe to
     run again
  5  The deploy is recorded and not live, because publishing is paused after a
     rollback

\e[1mEnvironment\e[0m
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_API\e[0m       The address of the API, as --api
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_SITE\e[0m      The site's id, as --site
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_KEY\e[0m       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `\e[1m\e[36mink\e[0m \e[1m\e[36mlogin\e[0m` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  \e[1m\e[36mINK_KEY_FILE\e[0m  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

\e[2mSee also\e[0m  \e[1m\e[36mink push\e[0m, \e[1m\e[36mink status\e[0m
\e[2mDocs\e[0m      \e[34mhttps://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md\e[0m
\e[2mGlobal\e[0m    \e[1m\e[36m-C,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--json,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m-q,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m-v,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--color,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--no-progress,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--log,\e[0m \e[1m\e[36m--log-file\e[0m
          \e[2m(see `ink --help`)\e[0m
